    "title": "Command execution via interpreter one-liner (GTFOBin)",
    "desc": "An interpreter was given an inline one-liner that runs a system command or spawns a shell - python -c 'import pty; pty.spawn(\"/bin/sh\")' or 'os.system(...)', perl -e 'exec \"/bin/sh\"', awk 'BEGIN{system(...)}', ruby -e 'system(\"/bin/sh\")'. This is the GTFOBins command/shell move for scripting languages (MITRE T1059 / T1202 Indirect Command Execution), scoped to the inline -c/-e form so a real script file (opaque, just a filename) is not guessed at. The socket/connect reverse-shell idioms are deliberately excluded - reverse_shell.yml owns those - so this is the non-network command-exec case.",
